  "notes": "Basis modified cash. Governmental lines use the Total Governmental Funds column (values printed on p6, labels on p5), which is already net of the Eliminations column (transfers of 230,000: 200,000 General to Depreciation via Building and grounds 100,000 and Pupil transportation 100,000; 30,000 General to Activity fund via Extracurricular activities), so top-level transfers are null and the statement roll-forward is 7,613,919 + 13,736,727 - 13,168,258 = 8,182,388. In the General Fund budget schedule (p9) the printed total disbursements 10,347,849 includes the 8000 Transfers 30,000 and 200,000 of transfers hidden in lines 2700 and building and grounds; the pupil transportation line was split (373,763 spending + 100,000 transfer), the building and grounds elimination is recorded as a contra expenditure line plus other financing, and the detail total is marked as including other financing. Depreciation Fund detail total receipts 245,706 includes the 200,000 transfer in. Activity (Other Governmental) fund has no detail schedule in the trimmed PDF. Business-type: Nutrition Fund (p7-p8); measure cash because the district reports on a modified cash basis and net position equals cash; beginning 264,914 and ending 175,721; reported business-type receipts total computed (operating 461,448 + interest 8,470). Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position (modified cash), Total column (includes Nutrition Fund cash 175,721); no liabilities. Page 3 is the right half of the Statement of Activities; p5/p6 are one statement split across two pages. Read pages 1-12 of 12."
}